WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:07.132
<i>She arrived like a monster.</i>

00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:09.884
<i>Sweeping away Puerto Rico entirely.</i>

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.970 line:0%
<i>Hurricane Maria would become</i>

00:00:12.053 --> 00:00:15.181
<i>the second deadliest hurricane
in US history.</i>

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:18.226
<i>FEMA came to my house.</i>

00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:19.894
<i>Two months later,</i>

00:00:19.978 --> 00:00:22.439 position:63%
<i>they told me, "No, you can't live here."</i>

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:27.569 position:56%
<i>One day I will go back to my island.</i>

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:31.990 line:0%
<i>Transitional Shelter Assistance
provides hotel rooms</i>

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:34.117 position:61% line:0%
<i>for displaced Puerto Ricans to live in.</i>

00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:37.120
<i>Six months, here at the hotel.</i>

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.663
<i>Give me a kiss!</i>

00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:41.207
<i>I met her here at the hotel.</i>

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:44.127
<i>They are like family to me.</i>

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.420
Move.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:51.509
<i>How do we get out of this city,
which is very difficult to live in?</i>

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.846
<i>FEMA is ending assistance
for Puerto Ricans</i>

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:56.014
<i>as many still struggle.</i>

00:00:56.598 --> 00:01:01.644 position:64%
Everybody's watching. They don't have
the guts to tell, "That's what happened."

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:04.189 position:59%
Now, where? That's what we don't know.

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:08.318
<i>I don't know if we will have
that help at hand.</i>

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:13.281 position:61%
<i>If they will help us get a place,
or if we're going to be in the streets.</i>

